{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b6870e0152657420", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{\n    \"query\": \"NA-BEATs noise-aware BEATs Fujimura IWAENC 2026 anomalous sound detection\",\n    \"follow_up_questions\": null,\n    \"answer\": \"NA-BEATs is a noise-aware audio representation learning method for detecting anomalous sounds. It uses self-supervised learning to extract clean representations from noisy signals. The method was presented in 2026 for the DCASE Challenge Task 2.\",\n    \"images\": [],\n    \"results\": [\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://www.merl.com/publications/docs/TR2026-100.pdf\",\n            \"title\": \"The MERL Systems for DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2\",\n            \"content\": \"T. Fujimura, I. Kuroyanagi, and T. Toda, \\u201cImprovements of discrim-inative feature space training for anomalous sound detection in unla-beled conditions,\\u201d in Proc. ICASSP, 2025.\\n T. Fujimura, Y. Masuyama, G. Wichern, C. Boeddeker, J. Richter, and J. Le Roux, \\u201cNABEATs: Noise-aware audio representation learning,\\u201d in Proc. IWAENC, (submitted), 2026.\\n S. Chen, Y. Wu, C. Wang, S. Liu, D. Tompkins, Z. Chen, W. Che, X. [...] MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC RESEARCH LABORATORIES  The MERL Systems for DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 4 Fujimura, Takuya; Wichern, Gordon; Masuyama, Yoshiki; Boeddeker, Christoph; Saijo, Kohei; Richter, Julius; Edo, Takahiro; Le Roux, Jonathan TR2026-100 July 01, 2026 Abstract In this report, we present our anomalous sound detection (ASD) systems for DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2. Our approach introduces noise-aware audio self-supervised learning (NA-SSL) to leverage two-channel recordings, in which one [...] Detection and Classification of Acoustic Scenes and Events 2026 Challenge 2. PRIOR WORK: NOISE-AWARE SELF-SUPERVISED LEARNING NA-SSL aims to extract clean SSL representations from noisy sig-nals by leveraging auxiliary noise information . As a specific realization, NA-BEATs has been proposed based on the widely used BEATs , where the auxiliary noise is obtained by crop-ping a noise-only segment from the noisy input signal . NA-BEATs is trained by distillation with a mean squared error (MSE)\",\n            \"score\": 0.82186085,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"1d01b7-00\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.16688\",\n            \"title\": \"NABEATs: Noise-Aware Audio Representation Learning\",\n            \"content\": \"by T Fujimura \\u00b7 2026 \\u00b7 Cited by 1 \\u2014 NABEATs is trained to estimate clean BEATs representations from a noisy audio signal with an auxiliary reference noise input. s significantly\",\n            \"score\": 0.7190094,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"a6564c-01\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://dcase.community/challenge2026/task-first-shot-unsupervised-anomalous-sound-detection-for-machine-condition-monitoring\",\n            \"title\": \"Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for ...\",\n            \"content\": \"Task open: 1st of April 2026\\n Additional training dataset release: 15th of May 2026\\n Evaluation dataset release: 1st of June 2026\\n External resource list lock: 1st of June 2026\\n Challenge deadline: 15th of June 2026\\n Challenge results: 30th of June 2026 [...] # Description\\n\\nAnomalous sound detection (ASD) is the task of identifying whether the sound emitted from a target machine is normal or anomalous. Automatic detection of mechanical failure is an essential technology in the fourth industrial revolution, which involves artificial-intelligence-based factory automation. Prompt detection of machine anomalies by observing sounds is useful for monitoring the condition of machines. Figure 1 shows an overview of the detection system. [...] Important: Notes on updating data file (8 April, 2026)  \\n Due to some data issues, the data file for ToyCar have 