{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a411b7bac56879be", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{\n    \"query\": \"DCASE 2026 challenge task 2 results leaderboard top systems\",\n    \"follow_up_questions\": null,\n    \"answer\": \"The MERL team won DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2, achieving top results in noise-aware anomalous sound detection. The final results were presented at the DCASE 2026 Workshop. The MERL team's system outperformed all other submissions.\",\n    \"images\": [],\n    \"results\": [\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://www.merl.com/news/award-20260630-1605\",\n            \"title\": \"MERL Team Wins DCASE 2026 Challenge on Anomalous Sound ...\",\n            \"content\": \"The MERL team won Task 2, Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring, which aims at building noise-robust systems for automatically detecting machine failure via microphones when only normal machine operating data is available for system development. Task 2 was by far the most popular out of the 7 DCASE 2026 tasks, with 51 teams submitting 168 entries. The MERL team's system was built around MERL\\u2019s recently proposed paradigm of noise-aware [...] MERL's Speech & Audio team ranked 1st out of 51 teams in the DCASE 2026 Challenge\\u2019s Task 2, \\u201cNoise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring.\\u201d The team was led by MERL intern Takuya Fujimura, and also included Gordon Wichern, Yoshiki Masuyama, Christoph Boeddeker, Kohei Saijo, Julius Richter, Takahiro Edo, and Jonathan Le Roux. [...] + Fujimura, T., Wichern, G., Masuyama, Y., Boeddeker, C., Saijo, K., Richter, J., Edo, T., Le Roux, J., \\\"The MERL Systems for DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2,\\\" Tech. Rep. TR2026-100, IEEE AASP Challenge on Detection and Classification of Acoustic Scenes and Events (DCASE Challenge), June 2026.\",\n            \"score\": 0.8616433,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"f0fa07-00\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://dcase.community/challenge2026/index\",\n            \"title\": \"DCASE2026 Challenge - DCASE\",\n            \"content\": \"| Task | Task description | Development dataset | Baseline system | Evaluation dataset | Results |\\n ---  ---  --- |\\n| Task 1, Heterogeneous Audio Classification | Released | Released | Released | Released | Released |\\n| Task 2, Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring | Released | Released | Released | Released | Released | [...] #### Organizers\\n\\nPanagiota Anastasopoulou\\n\\n#### Panagiota Anastasopoulou\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nFrederic Font\\n\\n#### Frederic Font\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nDmitry Bogdanov\\n\\n#### Dmitry Bogdanov\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nLonce Wyse\\n\\n#### Lonce Wyse\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nTask description Results\\n\\n## Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring\\n\\nMonitoring Task 2 [...] Daiki Takeuchi\\n\\n#### Daiki Takeuchi\\n\\nNTT, Inc.\\n\\nDaisuke Niizumi\\n\\n#### Daisuke Niizumi\\n\\nSB Intuitions Corp.\\n\\nKeisuke Imoto\\n\\n#### Keisuke Imoto\\n\\nKyoto University\\n\\nKota Dohi\\n\\n#### Kota Dohi\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nHarsh Purohit\\n\\n#### Harsh Purohit\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nTakashi Endo\\n\\n#### Takashi Endo\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nYohei Kawaguchi\\n\\n#### Yohei Kawaguchi\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nTask description Results\\n\\n## Semantic Acoustic Imaging for Sound Event Localization and Detection from Spatial Audio and Audiovisual Scenes\",\n            \"score\": 0.76300776,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"d5bd81-01\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2606.01578v1\",\n            \"title\": \"DESCRIPTION AND DISCUSSION ON DCASE 2026 CHALLENGE TASK 2: NOISE-AWARE UNSUPERVISED ANOMALOUS SOUND DETECTION FOR MACHINE CONDITION MONITORING\",\n            \"content\": \"## 5 Conclusion\\n\\nWe presented an overview of the DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2.\\nThe task aims to develop ASD systems that work under noisy conditions, given two-channel audio recordings recorded at different distances from the target machine.\\nResults and analysis of the challenge submissions will be added following the challenge submission deadline.\\n\\n## References [...] Tables 1 present the AUC and pAUC results for the two baseline systems on the development dataset, with the averages and standard deviations computed from five independent trials.\\n\\n## 4 Challenge Results\\n\\nWe will provide Challenge results and analysis of the submissions to the DCASE 2026 Workshop.\\n\\n## 5 Conclusion [...] where h\\u200b{\\u22c5}h\\\\left\\\\{\\\\cdot\\\\right\\\\} represents the harmonic mean, \\u2133\\\\mathcal{M} is the set of given machine types, and \\ud835\\udcae\\u200b(m)\\\\mathcal{S}(m) represents the set of sections for machine type mm.\\nSince the dataset in 2024, \\ud835\\udcae\\u200b(m)\\\\mathcal{S}(m) contains only 0000.\\n\\n### 3.3 Baseline systems and results\",\n            \"score\": 0.72348577,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"98a02f-02\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://biodcase.github.io/challenge2026/index\",\n            \"title\": \"BioDCASE Challenge - BioDCASE\",\n            \"content\": \"##### Challenge results published ##### 23 Oct 2026\\n\\n##### BioDCASE Workshop\\n\\n### Content\\n\\n Tasks\\n  + Multi-Channel Alignment\\n  + Supervised detection of strongly-labelled Antarctic blue and fin whale calls\\n  + Bioacoustics for Tiny Hardware\\n  + Active Learning for Bioacoustics\\n  + Cross-Domain Mosquito Species Classification\\n  + Bird Counting\\n\\n# Tasks [...] # Tasks\\n\\nResults are now available for the 2026 BioDCASE Challenge! Thank you to everyone who participated. See results pages for each task, linked below.\\n\\n## Multi-Channel Alignment\\n\\nAlignment Task 1 [...] The task is to estimate the number of individuals of the target species in each collection. The main leaderboard ranks systems based solely on target-species abundance estimation performance. Participants may optionally extend their methods to additional species; a secondary leaderboard showcases generalist systems estimating multiple species, but does not contribute to final rankings. Species detection itself is not evaluated; systems may use any detection strategy to focus on the target\",\n            \"score\": 0.68140936,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"6b6ba8-03\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://zenodo.org/records/20437238\",\n            \"title\": \"DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 Evaluation Dataset | Zenodo\",\n            \"content\": \"The focus of this year's task is on building noise-robust UASD systems by exploiting recordings captured simultaneously by multiple microphones placed at different distances from the target machine. Improving ASD performance in noisy conditions is essential for real-world deployment, since factory environments are acoustically complex with multiple machines operating simultaneously. However, achieving strong performance on noisy recordings remains challenging. [...] Directory structure\\n\\n- /eval\\\\_data\\n\\n    - /raw  \\n        - /ToyDrone  \\n            - /test   \\n                - /section\\\\_00\\\\_0001.wav    \\n                - ...    \\n                - /section\\\\_00\\\\_0199.wav\\n\\n       - /ToothBrush (The other machine types have the same directory structure as fan.)    \\n       - /SewingMachine  \\n       - /Blower  \\n       - /Sander\\n\\nBaseline system [...] This task is the follow-up from DCASE 2020 Task 2 to DCASE 2025 Task 2. The task this year is to develop an ASD system that meets the following five requirements.\",\n            \"score\": 0.65146625,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"5d1726-04\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"response_time\": 1.75,\n    \"request_id\": \"2038cc02-d8ee-48b0-8992-3e755e58292b\"\n}", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1357e959-003d-4f4f-9383-6abb9b9d2798", "uuid": "4c1b4d15-54db-4e6d-96c1-13076576b2d4", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T21:39:53.055Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "{\n    \"query\": \"DCASE 2026 challenge task 2 results leaderboard top systems\",\n    \"follow_up_questions\": null,\n    \"answer\": \"The MERL team won DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2, achieving top results in noise-aware anomalous sound detection. The final results were presented at the DCASE 2026 Workshop. The MERL team's system outperformed all other submissions.\",\n    \"images\": [],\n    \"results\": [\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://www.merl.com/news/award-20260630-1605\",\n            \"title\": \"MERL Team Wins DCASE 2026 Challenge on Anomalous Sound ...\",\n            \"content\": \"The MERL team won Task 2, Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring, which aims at building noise-robust systems for automatically detecting machine failure via microphones when only normal machine operating data is available for system development. Task 2 was by far the most popular out of the 7 DCASE 2026 tasks, with 51 teams submitting 168 entries. The MERL team's system was built around MERL\\u2019s recently proposed paradigm of noise-aware [...] MERL's Speech & Audio team ranked 1st out of 51 teams in the DCASE 2026 Challenge\\u2019s Task 2, \\u201cNoise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring.\\u201d The team was led by MERL intern Takuya Fujimura, and also included Gordon Wichern, Yoshiki Masuyama, Christoph Boeddeker, Kohei Saijo, Julius Richter, Takahiro Edo, and Jonathan Le Roux. [...] + Fujimura, T., Wichern, G., Masuyama, Y., Boeddeker, C., Saijo, K., Richter, J., Edo, T., Le Roux, J., \\\"The MERL Systems for DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2,\\\" Tech. Rep. TR2026-100, IEEE AASP Challenge on Detection and Classification of Acoustic Scenes and Events (DCASE Challenge), June 2026.\",\n            \"score\": 0.8616433,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"f0fa07-00\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://dcase.community/challenge2026/index\",\n            \"title\": \"DCASE2026 Challenge - DCASE\",\n            \"content\": \"| Task | Task description | Development dataset | Baseline system | Evaluation dataset | Results |\\n ---  ---  --- |\\n| Task 1, Heterogeneous Audio Classification | Released | Released | Released | Released | Released |\\n| Task 2, Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring | Released | Released | Released | Released | Released | [...] #### Organizers\\n\\nPanagiota Anastasopoulou\\n\\n#### Panagiota Anastasopoulou\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nFrederic Font\\n\\n#### Frederic Font\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nDmitry Bogdanov\\n\\n#### Dmitry Bogdanov\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nLonce Wyse\\n\\n#### Lonce Wyse\\n\\nUniversitat Pompeu Fabra\\n\\nTask description Results\\n\\n## Noise-aware Unsupervised Anomalous Sound Detection for Machine Condition Monitoring\\n\\nMonitoring Task 2 [...] Daiki Takeuchi\\n\\n#### Daiki Takeuchi\\n\\nNTT, Inc.\\n\\nDaisuke Niizumi\\n\\n#### Daisuke Niizumi\\n\\nSB Intuitions Corp.\\n\\nKeisuke Imoto\\n\\n#### Keisuke Imoto\\n\\nKyoto University\\n\\nKota Dohi\\n\\n#### Kota Dohi\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nHarsh Purohit\\n\\n#### Harsh Purohit\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nTakashi Endo\\n\\n#### Takashi Endo\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nYohei Kawaguchi\\n\\n#### Yohei Kawaguchi\\n\\nHitachi, Ltd.\\n\\nTask description Results\\n\\n## Semantic Acoustic Imaging for Sound Event Localization and Detection from Spatial Audio and Audiovisual Scenes\",\n            \"score\": 0.76300776,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"d5bd81-01\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2606.01578v1\",\n            \"title\": \"DESCRIPTION AND DISCUSSION ON DCASE 2026 CHALLENGE TASK 2: NOISE-AWARE UNSUPERVISED ANOMALOUS SOUND DETECTION FOR MACHINE CONDITION MONITORING\",\n            \"content\": \"## 5 Conclusion\\n\\nWe presented an overview of the DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2.\\nThe task aims to develop ASD systems that work under noisy conditions, given two-channel audio recordings recorded at different distances from the target machine.\\nResults and analysis of the challenge submissions will be added following the challenge submission deadline.\\n\\n## References [...] Tables 1 present the AUC and pAUC results for the two baseline systems on the development dataset, with the averages and standard deviations computed from five independent trials.\\n\\n## 4 Challenge Results\\n\\nWe will provide Challenge results and analysis of the submissions to the DCASE 2026 Workshop.\\n\\n## 5 Conclusion [...] where h\\u200b{\\u22c5}h\\\\left\\\\{\\\\cdot\\\\right\\\\} represents the harmonic mean, \\u2133\\\\mathcal{M} is the set of given machine types, and \\ud835\\udcae\\u200b(m)\\\\mathcal{S}(m) represents the set of sections for machine type mm.\\nSince the dataset in 2024, \\ud835\\udcae\\u200b(m)\\\\mathcal{S}(m) contains only 0000.\\n\\n### 3.3 Baseline systems and results\",\n            \"score\": 0.72348577,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"98a02f-02\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://biodcase.github.io/challenge2026/index\",\n            \"title\": \"BioDCASE Challenge - BioDCASE\",\n            \"content\": \"##### Challenge results published ##### 23 Oct 2026\\n\\n##### BioDCASE Workshop\\n\\n### Content\\n\\n Tasks\\n  + Multi-Channel Alignment\\n  + Supervised detection of strongly-labelled Antarctic blue and fin whale calls\\n  + Bioacoustics for Tiny Hardware\\n  + Active Learning for Bioacoustics\\n  + Cross-Domain Mosquito Species Classification\\n  + Bird Counting\\n\\n# Tasks [...] # Tasks\\n\\nResults are now available for the 2026 BioDCASE Challenge! Thank you to everyone who participated. See results pages for each task, linked below.\\n\\n## Multi-Channel Alignment\\n\\nAlignment Task 1 [...] The task is to estimate the number of individuals of the target species in each collection. The main leaderboard ranks systems based solely on target-species abundance estimation performance. Participants may optionally extend their methods to additional species; a secondary leaderboard showcases generalist systems estimating multiple species, but does not contribute to final rankings. Species detection itself is not evaluated; systems may use any detection strategy to focus on the target\",\n            \"score\": 0.68140936,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"6b6ba8-03\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"url\": \"https://zenodo.org/records/20437238\",\n            \"title\": \"DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 Evaluation Dataset | Zenodo\",\n            \"content\": \"The focus of this year's task is on building noise-robust UASD systems by exploiting recordings captured simultaneously by multiple microphones placed at different distances from the target machine. Improving ASD performance in noisy conditions is essential for real-world deployment, since factory environments are acoustically complex with multiple machines operating simultaneously. However, achieving strong performance on noisy recordings remains challenging. [...] Directory structure\\n\\n- /eval\\\\_data\\n\\n    - /raw  \\n        - /ToyDrone  \\n            - /test   \\n                - /section\\\\_00\\\\_0001.wav    \\n                - ...    \\n                - /section\\\\_00\\\\_0199.wav\\n\\n       - /ToothBrush (The other machine types have the same directory structure as fan.)    \\n       - /SewingMachine  \\n       - /Blower  \\n       - /Sander\\n\\nBaseline system [...] This task is the follow-up from DCASE 2020 Task 2 to DCASE 2025 Task 2. The task this year is to develop an ASD system that meets the following five requirements.\",\n            \"score\": 0.65146625,\n            \"raw_content\": null,\n            \"id\": \"5d1726-04\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"response_time\": 1.75,\n    \"request_id\": \"2038cc02-d8ee-48b0-8992-3e755e58292b\"\n}", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
